            <ArticleTitle>OCT-guided stenting of a spontaneous coronary artery dissection.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>301-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.carrev.2012.07.001</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1553-8389(12)00184-4</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present the case of a 67 year-old patient that presented to our institution with acute and severe chest pain. Optical coherence tomography high-resolution images of the coronary lumen, allowed us to confirm diagnosis of spontaneous coronary artery dissection, guide treatment, and verify the results of our intervention.</AbstractText>
